{%- comment -%}
  Main product section — generalized from "Product - fabU Skin Glow" design.
  The design's "Buy More, Save More" tier picker is promo/discount logic that can't
  be generalized to arbitrary products, so it is replaced by a quantity stepper.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
{%- assign on_sale = false -%}
{%- if current_variant.compare_at_price > current_variant.price -%}
  {%- assign on_sale = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign ingredients_mf = product.metafields.custom.ingredients -%}
{%- assign how_to_use_mf = product.metafields.custom.how_to_use -%}
{%- comment -%} A pharmacy-only product references a questionnaire metaobject here. When
    it does, the buy box is gated: no {% form 'product' %} is rendered (so with JS off the
    product cannot be added at all), and Add to bag opens the questionnaire instead. See
    the form block below and snippets/pharmacy-questionnaire.

    Three states, and the gate FAILS CLOSED. `pharma_mf` is the metafield itself, present
    whenever the merchant set it — even if its target metaobject was later deleted, when
    `.value` resolves to nil. So:
      - metafield absent      -> is_gated false -> normal buy box (an ordinary product)
      - metafield set, >=1 question -> gated, questionnaire shown
      - metafield set, target deleted or zero questions -> gated but NOT ready ->
        no buy box at all, a notice instead. Never a plain add-to-cart form.
    Keying "ready" off the resolved question count means a dangling reference and an
    empty questionnaire both fail the same safe way. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pharma_mf = product.metafields.pharmacy.questionnaire -%}
{%- assign questionnaire = pharma_mf.value -%}
{%- assign question_count = questionnaire.questions.value | size -%}
{%- assign is_gated = false -%}
{%- if pharma_mf != blank -%}{%- assign is_gated = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign gate_ready = false -%}
{%- if is_gated and question_count > 0 -%}{%- assign gate_ready = true -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} No metafield: the questions follow the restricted tag instead. Fergal
    adopted the old website's approach on 30 Sep 2026 (setup/old-site-questionnaires.md),
    which asks the same questions of a whole group rather than a set per product, so a
    medicine is covered the moment it is tagged and nobody has to remember a metafield.

    Which set is a tag too: `questionnaire-<set>` shows that set from
    snippets/pharmacy-question-set (ed, painkillers, ppi, ...). No set tag, or
    `questionnaire-none`, means no questions: Fergal's default since 1 Oct 2026. A set
    tag wins over `questionnaire-none`, so giving a medicine questions is one tag added.
    One set tag per product; with two, the first in tag order (alphabetical) wins. A
    set tag that names no set renders zero questions and so FAILS CLOSED, like an
    empty metaobject: a typo gates the product rather than opening it.
    A metaobject on the product still wins, so the pharmacist can override any of this
    per product later without touching the theme. Gating this way is the SAME gate: the
    branch below renders no product form either way, so a no-JS visitor still cannot add
    the medicine. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%} An empty string, not `blank`: LiquidJS in the preview harness does not
    treat `assign x = blank` as blank on the way back out, which gated a product that
    was meant to have no questions. Compare against the set names instead. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pq_set = '' -%}
{%- unless is_gated -%}
  {%- capture pq_restricted -%}{%- render 'product-restricted', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- if pq_restricted == 'true' -%}
    {%- assign pq_tags = product.tags | join: '||' | downcase | split: '||' -%}
    {%- for pq_tag in pq_tags -%}
      {%- assign pq_head = pq_tag | slice: 0, 14 -%}
      {%- if pq_head == 'questionnaire-' and pq_tag != 'questionnaire-none' -%}
        {%- assign pq_set = pq_tag | remove_first: 'questionnaire-' -%}
        {%- break -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if pq_set != '' -%}
      {%- assign is_gated = true -%}
      {%- comment -%} The button names the real number of questions, so the count has to
          come from the set rather than a word like "a few". `group::` items are section
          headings, not questions (snippets/pharmacy-questionnaire, "SECTION HEADINGS"),
          so they are skipped here too — otherwise turning grouping on would silently
          inflate the number on the button. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- capture pq_raw -%}{%- render 'pharmacy-question-set', set: pq_set -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign question_count = 0 -%}
      {%- assign pq_items = pq_raw | strip | split: '||' -%}
      {%- for pq_item in pq_items -%}
        {%- assign pq_kind = pq_item | strip | split: '::' | first -%}
        {%- unless pq_kind == 'group' -%}{%- assign question_count = question_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if question_count > 0 -%}{%- assign gate_ready = true -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endunless -%}

{%- comment -%} One label for both add buttons (buy box and mobile bar) and for the
    variant-change handler, so the three cannot drift. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture gate_label -%}Answer {{ question_count }} health question{% unless question_count == 1 %}s{% endunless %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- comment -%} The mobile bar's version. "Answer 18 health questions" beside the stepper
    ran 30-70px off the right edge of every phone from 320 to 414px; the count is on the
    buy box above, and the questionnaire's own header says "0 of 18 answered". {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign gate_label_short = 'Answer questions' -%}

{%- comment -%} The most specific collection this product belongs to. Shopify's
    product.collections ordering is arbitrary, so .first was picking a department as
    readily as a leaf. Used by the breadcrumb below and by the related-products
    fallback: a leaf is both a more useful trail and a tighter set of neighbours.
    A snippet cannot return an object, so it returns the handle. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture primary_handle -%}{%- render 'product-primary-collection', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign primary_handle = primary_handle | strip -%}
{%- assign primary_collection = blank -%}
{%- for c in product.collections -%}
  {%- if c.handle == primary_handle -%}
    {%- assign primary_collection = c -%}
    {%- break -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%} Related products: the most specific collection this product is in,
    and Shopify's recommendations only where there is no such collection.

    That order was the other way round until 1 Oct 2026, which made the rail's name a
    guess. `recommendations` is populated only in a section fetched through
    /recommendations/products?section_id=, and nothing fetches main-product that way —
    only sections/cart-recommendations, from theme.js. So on the live store the
    collection branch is the one that ran, every time, while the heading said
    "Have You Checked These Products Out?" and the preview harness (which sets
    recommendations.performed itself) exercised a branch the store never reached. The
    rail is now named after what it actually shows.

    Both rails below drop any product tagged settings.restricted_tag. A medicine is
    something a customer looks for and reads; it is not something to put in front of
    somebody who came for a moisturiser, and that holds on a medicine's own page too. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign rel = blank -%}
{%- assign rel_collection = blank -%}
{%- if primary_handle != blank and collections[primary_handle].products.size > 0 -%}
  {%- assign rel = collections[primary_handle].products -%}
  {%- assign rel_collection = primary_collection -%}
{%- elsif recommendations.performed and recommendations.products_count > 0 -%}
  {%- assign rel = recommendations.products -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- capture rail_heading -%}
  {%- if rel_collection != blank -%}More in {{ rel_collection.title }}{%- else -%}You might also like{%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign rail_heading = rail_heading | strip -%}

<div class="pdp-wrap-pad" style="width:100%; overflow-x:hidden; background:#ffffff;">

  <!-- Breadcrumb -->
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="max-width:1440px; margin:0 auto; padding:12px 30px 0;">
    <div class="crumb-trail{% if primary_collection != blank %} has-back{% endif %}" style="font-size:13px; color:#666b60; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:9px; align-items:center;">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="hov-green" style="color:#666b60;">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      {%- if primary_collection != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%} The collection's ancestors, from the same data as the
            BreadcrumbList, so the visible trail and the schema match. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- capture crumb_data -%}{%- render 'category-breadcrumb-data', collection: primary_collection -%}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- assign crumb_data = crumb_data | strip -%}
        {%- if crumb_data != blank -%}
          {%- assign crumbs = crumb_data | split: '|' -%}
          {%- for crumb in crumbs -%}
            {%- assign parts = crumb | split: '~' -%}
            <a href="/collections/{{ parts[1] }}" class="hov-green" style="color:#666b60;">{{ parts[0] | escape }}</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        <a href="{{ primary_collection.url }}" class="hov-green" style="color:#666b60;">{{ primary_collection.title }}</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span aria-current="page" style="color:#2A2B2A;">{{ product.title }}</span>
    </div>
    {%- if primary_collection != blank -%}
      {%- render 'crumb-back', url: primary_collection.url, title: primary_collection.title -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </nav>

  <!-- Main PDP -->
  <section id="pdp-{{ section.id }}" style="max-width:1440px; margin:0 auto; padding:22px 30px 8px;">
    <div class="pdp-cols" style="display:flex; gap:44px; align-items:flex-start;">

      <!-- LEFT: gallery + tabs -->
      <div class="pdp-left" style="flex:1 1 58%; min-width:0;">
        <div class="gallery-flex" style="display:flex; gap:18px;">
          {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
          <!-- Thumb rail -->
          <div class="thumb-railbox" style="flex:0 0 auto; display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; gap:12px;">
            <button type="button" class="thumb-nav pdp-thumb-nav" data-thumb-scroll="-1" aria-label="Previous images" style="width:36px; height:36px; border-radius:999px; border:1.5px solid #d9dbd6; background:#fff; color:var(--c-primary-text); cursor:pointer; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 15 12 9 18 15"></polyline></svg></button>
            <div class="thumb-rail" data-thumb-rail style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:12px; max-height:472px; overflow-y:auto; scrollbar-width:none;">
              {%- for media in product.media -%}
                <button type="button" class="thumb" data-pdp-thumb="{{ forloop.index0 }}" aria-label="View image {{ forloop.index }}" style="flex:0 0 auto; width:84px; height:84px; padding:6px; border-radius:9px; border:2px solid {% if forloop.first %}var(--c-primary){% else %}#e2e4df{% endif %}; background:#fff; cursor:pointer; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; overflow:hidden;">
                  {%- capture thumb_alt %}{% render 'image-alt', image: media.preview_image, product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
                  {{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 168 | image_tag: alt: thumb_alt, style: 'max-width:100%; max-height:100%; object-fit:contain; display:block;' }}
                </button>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
            <button type="button" class="thumb-nav pdp-thumb-nav" data-thumb-scroll="1" aria-label="More images" style="width:36px; height:36px; border-radius:999px; border:1.5px solid #d9dbd6; background:#fff; color:var(--c-primary-text); cursor:pointer; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></button>
          </div>
          {%- endif -%}
          <!-- Main image -->
          <div class="gallery-main" style="flex:1; min-width:0; position:relative; background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #eceee9; border-radius:14px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:28px; min-height:clamp(340px,42vw,560px);">
            {%- comment -%} Rendered whatever the first variant costs, hidden rather than
                omitted, so selecting a discounted variant can reveal it. It used to be
                emitted only when the first variant was on sale and never touched again:
                the strikethrough price followed the selection and this did not, so the
                page could show a SPECIAL OFFER flash over a variant with no offer, or
                hide one from a variant that had. {%- endcomment -%}
            <span data-pdp-badge style="position:absolute; top:20px; right:20px; background:var(--c-sale); color:#ffffff; font-weight:800; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:.06em; padding:8px 14px; border-radius:6px; {% unless on_sale %}display:none;{% endunless %}">SPECIAL OFFER</span>
            {%- if product.media.size > 0 -%}
              {%- for media in product.media -%}
                {%- capture main_alt %}{% render 'image-alt', image: media.preview_image, product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
                {%- comment -%} The first image is the LCP element on every product page: real srcset,
                    sizes matching the gallery column, eager + high priority + preload. The rest stay
                    lazy and are swapped in by theme.js via data-pdp-img. {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if forloop.first -%}
                  {%- comment -%} Written by hand, as the hero slider does. image_tag's preload argument
                      emitted nothing on the dev store, and a link carrying imagesrcset was dropped
                      from the served page; two media-scoped links, the pattern the slider already
                      uses, do render. 600 covers 85vw on phones at 2x, 1000 covers 43vw on desktop at 1x. {%- endcomment -%}
                  <link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 1000 }}" media="(min-width: 901px)" fetchpriority="high">
                  <link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 600 }}" media="(max-width: 900px)" fetchpriority="high">
                  {{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 1200 | image_tag:
                       widths: '400,600,800,1000,1200',
                       sizes: '(max-width: 900px) 85vw, 43vw',
                       alt: main_alt,
                       loading: 'eager',
                       fetchpriority: 'high',
                       data-pdp-img: forloop.index0,
                       style: 'width:70%; height:auto; display:block;' }}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 1200 | image_tag:
                       widths: '400,600,800,1000,1200',
                       sizes: '(max-width: 900px) 85vw, 43vw',
                       alt: main_alt,
                       loading: 'lazy',
                       data-pdp-img: forloop.index0,
                       style: 'width:70%; height:auto; display:block; display:none;' }}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- else -%}
              <div style="width:70%; aspect-ratio:1; border-radius:9px; background:repeating-linear-gradient(135deg,#dfe6d5,#dfe6d5 12px,#d7dfcb 12px,#d7dfcb 24px); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;"><span style="font-family:ui-monospace,monospace; font-size:11px; color:var(--c-primary-text); font-weight:700;">image</span></div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Description / How To Use / Ingredients tabs -->
        <div class="pdp-accordions" style="margin-top:34px;">
          <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0 8px; border-bottom:1px solid #e6e7e4;">
            <button type="button" class="pdp-tab" data-view-btn="desc" data-active="true">Description</button>
            {%- if how_to_use_mf != blank -%}
              <button type="button" class="pdp-tab" data-view-btn="how">How To Use</button>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if ingredients_mf != blank -%}
              <button type="button" class="pdp-tab" data-view-btn="ingredients">Ingredients</button>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <div data-view="desc" style="max-width:var(--measure); padding:22px 4px 26px; font-size:15.5px; line-height:1.7; color:#4a4d47;">{{ product.description }}</div>
          {%- if how_to_use_mf != blank -%}
            <div data-view="how" style="display:none; padding:22px 4px 26px; font-size:15.5px; line-height:1.7; color:#4a4d47;">{{ how_to_use_mf | metafield_tag }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if ingredients_mf != blank -%}
            <div data-view="ingredients" style="display:none; padding:22px 4px 26px; font-size:15.5px; line-height:1.7; color:#4a4d47;">{{ ingredients_mf | metafield_tag }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} Count what will actually render, not what is in the list. The loop
            skips the current product and caps at three, so a collection holding only this
            product passes `rel.size > 0` and then draws the heading over nothing - the
            same defect the brands page had. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign rel_count = 0 -%}
        {%- if rel != blank -%}
          {%- for p in rel -%}
            {%- capture p_restricted -%}{%- render 'product-restricted', product: p -%}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- unless p.id == product.id or p_restricted == 'true' -%}{%- assign rel_count = rel_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endunless -%}
            {%- if rel_count >= 3 -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if rel_count > 0 -%}
        <!-- You may also like: in the buy column beside the tabs from 1101px, under the description below that -->
        <div class="pdp-recs" style="margin-top:34px; max-width:600px;">
        <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-heading); font-weight:800; color:var(--c-dark); font-size:24px; margin:0 0 20px;">You may also like</h2>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:6px;">
          {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
          {%- for p in rel -%}
            {%- capture restricted -%}{%- render 'product-restricted', product: p -%}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- assign restricted = restricted | strip -%}
            {%- if p.id == product.id or restricted == 'true' or shown >= 3 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
            {%- comment -%} Blank unless the price shown is genuinely reduced — see snippets/product-compare-at.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- capture was -%}{%- render 'product-compare-at', product: p -%}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- assign was = was | strip -%}
            <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:16px; padding:14px 0; border-bottom:1px solid #eceee9;">
              <a href="{% render 'product-card-url', product: p %}" style="flex:0 0 92px; height:92px; border-radius:10px; background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #eceee9; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; overflow:hidden;">
                {%- if p.featured_image -%}
                  {%- capture rel_alt %}{% render 'image-alt', image: p.featured_image, product: p %}{% endcapture -%}
                  {{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 184 | image_tag: alt: rel_alt, style: 'max-width:84%; max-height:84%; object-fit:contain; display:block;', loading: 'lazy' }}
                {%- else -%}
                  <div style="width:80%; height:80%; border-radius:7px; background:repeating-linear-gradient(135deg,#dfe6d5,#dfe6d5 12px,#d7dfcb 12px,#d7dfcb 24px);"></div>
                {%- endif -%}
              </a>
              <div style="flex:1; min-width:0;">
                <h3 style="font-weight:700; font-size:15px; line-height:1.3; margin:0 0 6px;"><a href="{% render 'product-card-url', product: p %}" class="hov-green" style="color:#2A2B2A;">{{ p.title }}</a></h3>
                <div style="margin-bottom:6px;">{% render 'product-rating', product: p, size: 13, count_label: 'long' %}</div>
                <div style="display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:8px;"><span style="color:var(--c-primary-text); font-weight:800; font-size:17px;">{{ p.price | money }}</span>{%- if was != blank -%}<span class="price-was" style="font-size:13.5px;">{{ was }}</span>{%- endif -%}</div>
              </div>
              {%- if p.available and p.has_only_default_variant -%}
                <button type="button" data-add-id="{{ p.first_available_variant.id }}" class="btn-sm btn-fill" style="flex:0 0 auto; align-self:center">Add</button>
              {%- else -%}
                <a href="{% render 'product-card-url', product: p %}" class="btn-sm btn-fill" style="flex:0 0 auto; align-self:center">View</a>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
        </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} Renders nothing at all until the FAQ metafield holds content.
            Below the tabs rather than inside them: the answers have to stay in the
            DOM to be eligible for the rich result. {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'product-faq', product: product %}
      </div>

      <!-- RIGHT: info -->
      <div class="pdp-right" style="flex:0 0 400px; width:400px;">
        {%- comment -%} Same as the gallery badge: present but hidden, so it can follow
            the selected variant instead of freezing on the first one. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div data-pdp-offer style="display:{% if on_sale %}inline-flex{% else %}none{% endif %}; align-items:center; gap:8px; background:var(--c-tint); color:var(--c-text); font-weight:700; font-size:13.5px; padding:9px 20px; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:18px;">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 12v9H4v-9"></path><rect x="2" y="7" width="20" height="5" rx="1"></rect><path d="M12 22V7M12 7H7.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 0-5C11 2 12 7 12 7zM12 7h4.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 0 0-5C13 2 12 7 12 7z"></path></svg>
          Special Offer
        </div>
        {%- if product.vendor != blank -%}
          <div style="font-size:14px; font-weight:700; color:var(--c-primary-text); margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="{{ product.vendor | url_for_vendor }}" class="hov-green-dk" style="color:var(--c-primary-text);">{{ product.vendor }}</a></div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <h1 style="font-family:var(--font-body); font-weight:800; color:var(--c-dark); font-size:clamp(26px,2.8vw,34px); line-height:1.12; margin:0 0 10px;">{{ product.title }}</h1>
        {%- if current_variant.sku != blank -%}
          <div data-pdp-sku style="font-size:14px; color:var(--c-muted-2); margin-bottom:10px;">SKU {{ current_variant.sku }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <div style="margin-bottom:18px;">{% render 'product-rating', product: product, size: 16, count_label: 'long', link: '#product-reviews' %}</div>
        <div style="display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:14px; margin-bottom:12px;">
          <span data-pdp-price style="font-family:var(--font-body); color:var(--c-primary-text); font-weight:800; font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);">{{ current_variant.price | money }}</span>
          <span data-pdp-compare style="font-weight:600; font-size:clamp(17px,1.8vw,22px); color:#666b60; text-decoration:line-through; {% unless on_sale %}display:none;{% endunless %}">{{ current_variant.compare_at_price | money }}</span>
        </div>
        {%- capture promo -%}{%- render 'product-promo-label', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- assign promo = promo | strip -%}
        {%- if promo != blank -%}<div style="margin-bottom:18px;"><span class="promo-label">{{ promo }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%} The gift offers need a sentence the chip cannot carry: a free
            gift is only free once the customer puts it in the bag, because Shopify
            discounts a gift in the cart and never adds it there. PDP only — a card has
            no room for it, and the chip already says an offer exists. Rich text so the
            link to the gift lives with the copy instead of being built here.
            MAINTENANCE.md, "The multi-buy offers are automatic discounts". {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign promo_note = product.metafields.custom.promo_note -%}
        {%- if promo_note != blank -%}
          <div class="promo-note">{{ promo_note | metafield_tag }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <div data-pdp-stock style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; font-size:14px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:24px; color:{% if current_variant.available %}var(--c-success){% else %}#B3261E{% endif %};">
          <span style="width:9px; height:9px; border-radius:999px; background:currentColor;"></span>
          {% if current_variant.available %}In stock — ready to ship{% else %}Out of stock{% endif %}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} The variant controls are identical whether or not the product is
            gated, so they are captured once and emitted into whichever buy box renders.
            The hidden id input starts disabled on a multi-variant product (the script
            below enables it) so a no-JS submit sends no id rather than the wrong one, and
            the option selects cannot name a variant on their own — /cart/add resolves an
            `id`, never option values. The noscript variant picker is the no-JS buy path
            and so is dropped for a gated product, which must have no no-JS buy path at
            all. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- capture variant_selects -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ current_variant.id }}"{% unless product.has_only_default_variant %} disabled data-pdp-id{% endunless %}>
          {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
            {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
              {%- assign opt_i = forloop.index0 -%}
              <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
                <label for="Opt-{{ section.id }}-{{ opt_i }}" style="display:block; font-size:13.5px; font-weight:700; color:#2A2B2A; margin-bottom:8px;">{{ option.name }}</label>
                <select id="Opt-{{ section.id }}-{{ opt_i }}" data-opt-index="{{ opt_i }}" style="width:100%; height:52px; border:1.5px solid #dfe1dc; border-radius:11px; padding:0 14px; font-family:inherit; font-size:15px; color:#2A2B2A; background:#fff; cursor:pointer;">
                  {%- for value in option.values -%}
                    <option value="{{ value | escape }}" {% if current_variant.options[opt_i] == value %}selected{% endif %}>{{ value }}</option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- unless is_gated -%}
              <noscript>
                <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
                  <label for="NoJsVariant-{{ section.id }}" style="display:block; font-size:13.5px; font-weight:700; color:#2A2B2A; margin-bottom:8px;">Choose an option</label>
                  <select id="NoJsVariant-{{ section.id }}" name="id" style="width:100%; height:52px; border:1.5px solid #dfe1dc; border-radius:11px; padding:0 14px; font-family:inherit; font-size:15px; color:#2A2B2A; background:#fff;">
                    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
                      <option value="{{ variant.id }}"{% if variant.id == current_variant.id %} selected{% endif %}{% unless variant.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>{{ variant.title }} — {{ variant.price | money }}{% unless variant.available %} (out of stock){% endunless %}</option>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </select>
                </div>
              </noscript>
            {%- endunless -%}
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}
        {%- capture qty_stepper -%}
          <div style="flex:0 0 auto; display:flex; align-items:center; border:1.5px solid #dfe1dc; border-radius:12px; overflow:hidden;">
            <button type="button" data-qty-step="-1" disabled aria-label="Decrease quantity" style="width:46px; height:100%; border:none; background:#fff; color:#2A2B2A; font-size:22px; cursor:pointer; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">−</button>
            <input type="text" name="quantity" value="1" inputmode="numeric" data-pdp-qty aria-label="Quantity" style="width:44px; border:none; text-align:center; font-weight:700; font-size:16px; color:var(--c-primary-text); outline:none; background:#fff;">
            <button type="button" data-qty-step="1" aria-label="Increase quantity" style="width:46px; height:100%; border:none; background:#fff; color:#2A2B2A; font-size:22px; cursor:pointer; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">+</button>
          </div>
        {%- endcapture -%}

        {%- comment -%} A gift card is bought on /pages/gift-vouchers and nowhere else.
            That page is the only thing that collects the amount, the delivery method,
            the recipient and the send date, and those become the line item properties
            Shopify reads to issue the voucher and email it. This page could post a
            bare {% form 'product' %} with none of them, and Shopify would quietly issue
            the voucher to the buyer instead of the person it was meant for — no error,
            no clue, just the wrong recipient. So there is no form here at all: with
            nothing to POST, a no-JS visitor cannot bypass it either, the same reasoning
            as the gated medicine box below. product-restricted.liquid stops the
            one-click add on every card, and product-card-url.liquid points those cards
            here; all three have to agree. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if product.gift_card? -%}
          <div class="pdp-buybox">
            <p style="margin:0 0 16px; font-size:15.5px; line-height:1.65; color:#5d6159;">Choose an amount, say who it&rsquo;s for and when it should arrive on the gift vouchers page.</p>
            <a href="/pages/gift-vouchers" class="btn btn-fill" style="gap:10px; width:100%; margin-bottom:18px;">Buy a gift voucher</a>
          </div>
        {%- elsif is_gated == false -%}
          {% form 'product', product, data-ajax-add: 'true' %}
            {{ variant_selects }}
            <div class="pdp-addbag" style="display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:stretch; margin-bottom:18px;">
              {{ qty_stepper }}
              <button type="submit" data-pdp-submit class="btn btn-fill" {% unless current_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %} style="flex:1; gap:11px; letter-spacing:.06em; {% unless current_variant.available %}opacity:.55; {% endunless %}">
                {%- if current_variant.available %}ADD TO BAG{% else %}OUT OF STOCK{% endif -%}
              </button>
            </div>
            {% render 'wishlist-button', product: product, style: 'text' %}
            {%- comment -%} Shopify's accelerated checkout button (Shop Pay / Apple Pay / …).
                Skips the cart entirely for a shopper who just wants this one item. Behind a
                setting because it can cannibalise cart-based upsell — switch it off in the
                editor rather than editing code. Renders nothing in the mock preview.
                Never on a medicine: Buy it now skips the bag, and the bag is where the
                customer confirms they are over 18 and will follow the leaflet (PSI 2.5,
                sections/main-cart.liquid). The Flow flags an order that skipped it
                anyway; this only stops the theme offering the skip. {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- capture self_restricted -%}{%- render 'product-restricted', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if section.settings.show_dynamic_checkout and current_variant.available and self_restricted != 'true' -%}
              <div class="pdp-express" style="margin-top:12px;">
                {{ form | payment_button }}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {% endform %}
        {%- elsif gate_ready -%}
          {%- comment -%} Gated buy box. Deliberately NOT a {% form 'product' %}: with no
              form there is nothing to POST, so a no-JS visitor cannot add this medicine at
              all — the gate Inish leave open. The button is type=button and opens the
              questionnaire; the express checkout button is omitted because it would skip
              the questionnaire entirely. The same data-* hooks are used, so the variant
              script below still drives the id, price and stock. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="pdp-buybox" data-gated-buybox>
            {{ variant_selects }}
            <div class="pdp-addbag" style="display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:stretch; margin-bottom:18px;">
              {{ qty_stepper }}
              <button type="button" data-pdp-submit data-open-questionnaire aria-haspopup="dialog" class="btn btn-fill" {% unless current_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %} style="flex:1; gap:11px; letter-spacing:.04em; {% unless current_variant.available %}opacity:.55; {% endunless %}">
                {%- if current_variant.available %}{{ gate_label }}{% else %}OUT OF STOCK{% endif -%}
              </button>
            </div>
            {% render 'wishlist-button', product: product, style: 'text' %}
          </div>
          {% render 'pharmacy-questionnaire', product: product, questionnaire: questionnaire, set: pq_set, section_id: section.id, variant: current_variant %}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%} Gated, but the questionnaire is missing (reference deleted) or has
              no questions. Fail CLOSED: no buy box, no form, no add path — just a notice.
              A pharmacy product must never drop back to a plain add-to-cart when its
              screening is not there to run. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="pdp-buybox" data-gated-unavailable role="status" style="border:1.5px solid #e6c7c4; background:#fbeceb; border-radius:14px; padding:18px 20px; margin-bottom:18px;">
            <div style="font-weight:800; color:#8a1f18; font-size:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">Not available to buy online right now</div>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.6; color:#4a4d47;">This is a pharmacy medicine and its pharmacist questions aren’t set up yet, so it can’t be added to the bag. Please <a href="/pages/contact-us" style="color:var(--c-primary-text); font-weight:700;">ask our pharmacist</a> and we’ll help you directly.</div>
          </div>
          {% render 'wishlist-button', product: product, style: 'text' %}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%} Outside the product form deliberately: a contact form cannot be
            nested inside another form, and this is the one case where the buy box has
            nothing to sell. Off by default (show_back_in_stock) until the client
            confirms who owns the contact inbox and a live submission has been tested;
            the snippet and its checks stay in place for when it is switched back on. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.show_back_in_stock and current_variant.available == false -%}
          {% render 'back-in-stock', product: product, variant: current_variant %}
        {%- endif -%}
        <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; font-size:15px; color:#2A2B2A; margin-bottom:34px;">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="var(--c-accent)" style="flex:0 0 auto;"><path d="M3 5.75A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 4.75 4h8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 15 5.75V6h2.6c.5 0 .96.24 1.25.64l2.4 3.3c.16.22.25.49.25.76V15a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5h-.6a2.75 2.75 0 0 1-5.4 0H10.4a2.75 2.75 0 0 1-5.4 0h-.25A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 3 14.75V5.75ZM15 7.5v3.5h4v-.32L16.9 7.8a.5.5 0 0 0-.4-.2H15ZM7.7 15.75a1.25 1.25 0 1 0-2.5 0 1.25 1.25 0 0 0 2.5 0Zm9.6 0a1.25 1.25 0 1 0-2.5 0 1.25 1.25 0 0 0 2.5 0Z"></path></svg>
          <span><strong style="font-weight:800;">Free delivery</strong> on orders over {% render 'free-delivery-amount' %}</span>
        </div>
        {%- comment -%} Dispatch, collection and pharmacist reassurance, where the
            decision is actually being made. Was footer-only. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div style="margin:-22px 0 32px;">
          {% render 'buy-assurance', variant: current_variant, product: product, all_products: section.settings.show_pharmacy_lines %}
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%}
    Landing zone for the review app. Install the app, then in the theme editor
    add its block here — the star rating above links to this anchor. Empty
    until an app block is added, so nothing shows on a store without reviews.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section id="product-reviews" style="max-width:1440px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 30px; scroll-margin-top:130px;">
    {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
      {%- if block.type == '@app' -%}
        <div style="padding:44px 0 8px;">{% render block %}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} Count what will actually be drawn: the loop skips this product and
      every medicine, so a collection of one plus a shelf of pharmacy lines would
      otherwise draw the heading over an empty track — the defect the brands page had,
      and the reason the side list above counts first too. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign rail_count = 0 -%}
  {%- if rel != blank -%}
    {%- for p in rel -%}
      {%- capture p_restricted -%}{%- render 'product-restricted', product: p -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- unless p.id == product.id or p_restricted == 'true' -%}{%- assign rail_count = rail_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endunless -%}
      {%- if rail_count >= 8 -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if rail_count > 0 -%}
  <!-- More in <collection> -->
  <section style="max-width:1440px; margin:0 auto; padding:var(--sec-pad-top) 30px var(--sec-pad-bottom);">
    <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-heading); font-weight:800; color:var(--c-dark); font-size:clamp(24px,2.6vw,32px); margin:0 0 26px;">{{ rail_heading }}</h2>
    <div style="position:relative;">
      <div id="checked-track-{{ section.id }}" style="display:flex; gap:22px; overflow-x:auto; scroll-behavior:smooth; scrollbar-width:none; padding:4px;">
        {%- assign railshown = 0 -%}
        {%- for p in rel -%}
          {%- capture restricted -%}{%- render 'product-restricted', product: p -%}{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- if p.id == product.id or restricted == 'true' or railshown >= 8 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- assign railshown = railshown | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- render 'product-card', product: p, width: '254px' -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
      <button aria-label="Scroll back" data-rail-btn data-rail-back data-rail-target="checked-track-{{ section.id }}" data-rail-by="-552" class="hov-bg-green-dk" style="position:absolute; left:-14px; top:38%; transform:translateY(-50%); width:46px; height:46px; border-radius:999px; border:none; background:var(--c-primary); color:var(--c-on-primary); cursor:pointer; display:none; align-items:center; justify-content:center; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.15);"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="15 6 9 12 15 18"></polyline></svg></button>
      <button aria-label="Scroll forward" data-rail-btn data-rail-target="checked-track-{{ section.id }}" data-rail-by="552" class="hov-bg-green-dk" style="position:absolute; right:-14px; top:38%; transform:translateY(-50%); width:46px; height:46px; border-radius:999px; border:none; background:var(--c-primary); color:var(--c-on-primary); cursor:pointer; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.15);"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 6 15 12 9 18"></polyline></svg></button>
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  <!-- Mobile sticky add-to-bag bar -->
  <div class="mobile-buybar" style="display:none; position:fixed; left:0; right:0; bottom:0; z-index:150; background:#ffffff; border-top:1px solid #e6e7e4; box-shadow:0 -6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.08); padding:12px 16px; gap:12px; align-items:stretch;">
    <div style="flex:0 0 auto; display:flex; align-items:center; border:1.5px solid #dfe1dc; border-radius:11px; overflow:hidden;">
      <button type="button" data-qty-step="-1" disabled aria-label="Decrease quantity" style="width:44px; border:none; background:#fff; color:#2A2B2A; font-size:22px; cursor:pointer; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">−</button>
      <span data-buybar-qty style="min-width:26px; text-align:center; font-weight:700; font-size:16px; color:var(--c-primary-text);">1</span>
      <button type="button" data-qty-step="1" aria-label="Increase quantity" style="width:44px; border:none; background:#fff; color:#2A2B2A; font-size:22px; cursor:pointer; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">+</button>
    </div>
    {%- comment -%} On a gated product this bar opens the questionnaire too, rather than
        quick-adding: a [data-add-id] button would post straight to /cart/add.js and skip
        the gate. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if product.gift_card? -%}
      <a href="/pages/gift-vouchers" class="btn btn-fill buybar-btn" style="flex:1; gap:10px; letter-spacing:.05em;">Buy a gift voucher</a>
    {%- elsif is_gated == false -%}
      <button type="button" data-add-id="{{ current_variant.id }}" data-add-qty="1" data-buybar-add class="btn btn-fill buybar-btn" {% unless current_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %} style="flex:1; gap:10px; letter-spacing:.05em; {% unless current_variant.available %}opacity:.55; {% endunless %}">
        <svg class="buybar-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 2 3 6v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V6l-3-4z"></path><path d="M3 6h18"></path><path d="M16 10a4 4 0 0 1-8 0"></path></svg>
        <span data-buybar-label>{%- if current_variant.available %}ADD TO BAG{% else %}OUT OF STOCK{% endif -%}</span>
      </button>
    {%- elsif gate_ready -%}
      <button type="button" data-open-questionnaire aria-haspopup="dialog" class="btn btn-fill buybar-btn" {% unless current_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %} style="flex:1; gap:10px; letter-spacing:.04em; {% unless current_variant.available %}opacity:.55; {% endunless %}">
        <svg class="buybar-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 2 3 6v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V6l-3-4z"></path><path d="M3 6h18"></path><path d="M16 10a4 4 0 0 1-8 0"></path></svg>
        <span data-buybar-label>{%- if current_variant.available %}{{ gate_label_short }}{% else %}OUT OF STOCK{% endif -%}</span>
      </button>
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%} Fail closed on mobile too: a disabled button, never a working add. {%- endcomment -%}
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-fill buybar-btn" disabled style="flex:1; gap:10px; letter-spacing:.04em; opacity:.55;">
        <span>Ask our pharmacist</span>
      </button>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

</div>

{% style %}
  /* Under 360px the bag icon goes, so "Answer questions" fits beside the stepper. */
  @media (max-width: 359px) {
    .mobile-buybar .buybar-icon { display: none; }
    .mobile-buybar .buybar-btn { padding-left: 10px; padding-right: 10px; letter-spacing: 0 !important; }
  }
  .pcard:hover .pcard-img img { transform: scale(1.04); transition: transform .3s ease; }
  .pdp-thumb-nav:hover { border-color: var(--c-accent) !important; background: #f2f8e9 !important; }
  .pdp-tab {
    background: transparent; border: none; cursor: pointer; padding: 12px 14px 14px;
    font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 700; color: var(--c-dark);
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.7vw, 20px); border-bottom: 3px solid transparent; margin-bottom: -1px;
  }
  .pdp-tab:not([data-active="true"]):hover { color:var(--c-primary-text); }
  [data-qty-step]:hover:not(:disabled) { background: #f4f5f2 !important; }
  [data-qty-step]:disabled { opacity: .4; cursor: default; }
  .pdp-tab[data-active="true"] { color:var(--c-primary-text); border-bottom-color:var(--c-primary-text); }
  /* Wide desktop: a grid, so "You May Also Like" sits in the 400px buy column
     level with the tabs, below Add To Bag rather than beside it. Row 1 is the
     gallery and the buy box, row 2 the tabs and the list, row 3 the FAQ. The
     description keeps its --measure cap. Below 1101 the left column is too narrow
     to give up, so the list stays under the description (the flex layout above).
     If a buy box ever runs taller than the gallery, row 2 starts under the buy
     box, leaving a gap under the gallery; that is the cost of the tabs and the
     list starting level. See MAINTENANCE, "You May Also Like". */
  @media (min-width: 1101px) {
    .pdp-cols { display: grid !important; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 400px; column-gap: 44px; }
    .pdp-left { display: contents !important; }
    .gallery-flex { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1; }
    .pdp-right { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1; width: auto !important; }
    .pdp-accordions { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 2; }
    .pdp-recs { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 2; max-width: none !important; }
    .pfaq { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 3; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 940px) {
    .pdp-cols { flex-direction: column !important; align-items: stretch !important; gap: 24px !important; }
    .pdp-left { display: contents !important; }
    .pdp-right { flex: 1 1 auto !important; width: 100% !important; order: 2 !important; }
    .gallery-flex { order: 1 !important; width: 100% !important; }
    .pdp-accordions { order: 3 !important; width: 100% !important; }
    /* The recs and FAQ live in .pdp-left too; display:contents releases them
       into the flex order, and without their own order they sort to 0 - above
       the gallery. 4 and 5 keep them after the description, matching desktop. */
    .pdp-recs { order: 4 !important; width: 100% !important; }
    .pfaq { order: 5 !important; width: 100% !important; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .mobile-buybar { display: flex !important; }
    /* The button takes what the stepper leaves and no more: min-width:0 lets it shrink
       below its nowrap label, and the label clips rather than pushing off-screen. */
    .mobile-buybar .buybar-btn { min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; }
    .mobile-buybar .buybar-btn > span { overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
    /* The bag drawer opens over this page. The drawer lives in the header group, a
       stacking context at z-index 150, so its own 301 cannot lift it over this bar
       (also 150, later in the DOM) - the bar sat on the drawer's Checkout and a tap
       there added the product again. Hide the bar while the drawer is open. */
    body[data-cd-open] .mobile-buybar { visibility: hidden; }
    /* While the consent banner is open it fully overlaps the fixed buy bar
       (z-index 400 vs 150) - hide the bar rather than leave dead pixels
       behind the banner. visibility keeps it mounted, so no reflow; the
       150ms visibility delay plus 300ms fade stops the Accept tap - at the
       same y as ADD TO BAG - from landing on a bar that appears under a
       lifting finger. */
    .mobile-buybar { transition: opacity .3s ease .15s, visibility 0s linear .15s; }
    body:has([data-cc-banner]:not([hidden])) .mobile-buybar { visibility: hidden; opacity: 0; transition: none; }
    body { padding-bottom: 82px; } /* keep footer content clear of the fixed buybar */
    .pdp-addbag { display: none !important; }
    .thumb-nav { display: none !important; }
    .thumb-railbox { width: 100% !important; }
    .gallery-main { min-height: 320px !important; padding: 22px !important; }
    .gallery-flex { flex-direction: column-reverse !important; }
    .thumb-rail { flex-direction: row !important; width: 100% !important; overflow-x: auto !important; max-height: none !important; }
    .thumb-rail .thumb { flex: 0 0 74px !important; }
    /* The rail's cards are the shared snippet now, which sets its width inline;
       .checked-card no longer exists. Target them through the track. */
    #checked-track-{{ section.id }} > .prodcard { flex: 0 0 44% !important; }
  }
{% endstyle %}

{%- comment -%} Must come BEFORE the script below, which is an IIFE that runs at
    parse time. This block used to sit after it, so getElementById returned null and
    the variant picker never worked at all: selecting a size changed no price, no SKU
    and no hidden variant id. It went unnoticed because no multi-variant product
    rendered in any preview until the fixture was added. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
  <script type="application/json" id="pdp-variants-{{ section.id }}">{{ product.variants | json }}</script>
  {%- comment -%} Which gallery frame belongs to which variant, as "id:index,id:index".
      featured_media.position is 1-based over product.media and the frames above are
      stamped with forloop.index0, so the frame index is position - 1. A flat string
      rather than JSON because a variant without its own media contributes no pair,
      and building valid JSON around the gaps costs more Liquid than parsing this
      costs JavaScript. Variants with no media of their own are simply absent, and
      the gallery then stays where it is. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign variant_media = '' -%}
  {%- for v in product.variants -%}
    {%- if v.featured_media -%}
      {%- assign frame = v.featured_media.position | minus: 1 -%}
      {%- assign variant_media = variant_media | append: v.id | append: ':' | append: frame | append: ',' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  <span data-pdp-variant-media="{{ variant_media }}" hidden></span>
{%- endunless -%}
<script>
  (() => {
    const root = document.getElementById('pdp-{{ section.id }}');
    if (!root) return;

    // Gallery: thumb click swaps main image
    const mains = [...document.querySelectorAll('[data-pdp-img]')];
    const thumbs = [...root.querySelectorAll('[data-pdp-thumb]')];
    const showImg = i => {
      mains.forEach(img => { img.style.display = img.dataset.pdpImg == i ? 'block' : 'none'; });
      thumbs.forEach(t => { t.style.borderColor = t.dataset.pdpThumb == i ? 'var(--c-primary)' : '#e2e4df'; });
    };
    if (mains.length > 1) showImg(0);
    thumbs.forEach(t => t.addEventListener('click', () => showImg(t.dataset.pdpThumb)));
    root.querySelectorAll('[data-thumb-scroll]').forEach(btn => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const rail = root.querySelector('[data-thumb-rail]');
        if (rail) rail.scrollBy({ top: 96 * btn.dataset.thumbScroll, left: 86 * btn.dataset.thumbScroll, behavior: 'smooth' });
      });
    });

    // Quantity stepper (main form + mobile buybar stay in sync)
    const qtyInput = root.querySelector('[data-pdp-qty]');
    const buybarQty = document.querySelector('[data-buybar-qty]');
    const buybarAdd = document.querySelector('[data-buybar-add]');
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-qty-step]').forEach(btn => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const q = Math.max(1, (parseInt(qtyInput.value, 10) || 1) + parseInt(btn.dataset.qtyStep, 10));
        document.querySelectorAll('[data-qty-step="-1"]').forEach(b => { b.disabled = q <= 1; });
        qtyInput.value = q;
        if (buybarQty) buybarQty.textContent = q;
        if (buybarAdd) buybarAdd.dataset.addQty = q;
      });
    });

    // Variant selects -> hidden id + price/sku/stock
    const sels = [...root.querySelectorAll('[data-opt-index]')];
    if (!sels.length) return;
    const idInput = root.querySelector('input[name="id"]');
    // Enabled only now: the markup ships it disabled so a page whose script never
    // runs submits no id at all instead of the wrong one. See the comment there.
    if (idInput) idInput.disabled = false;
    const variants = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('pdp-variants-{{ section.id }}').textContent);
    // The store's money format, from theme.js. Called only on a variant change, after the
    // deferred theme.js has run.
    const fmt = c => window.mccFormatMoney(c);
    const submit = root.querySelector('[data-pdp-submit]');
    const buybarLabel = document.querySelector('[data-buybar-label]');

    // Both add controls move together. A combination no variant covers is its own
    // state, not a flavour of sold out, and it used to leave the sticky mobile bar
    // untouched: the handler returned early, so the bar kept the last valid variant
    // id, stayed enabled and added a different product without saying anything.
    // On a gated product [data-pdp-submit] is the questionnaire opener, not an add
    // button, so relabelling it 'ADD TO BAG' on a variant change left a button that
    // said one thing and did another. The available label follows the gate.
    const addLabel = {% if is_gated %}{{ gate_label | json }}{% else %}'ADD TO BAG'{% endif %};
    const barLabel = {% if is_gated %}{{ gate_label_short | json }}{% else %}'ADD TO BAG'{% endif %};
    const setBuy = (v) => {
      const live = !!v && v.available;
      const label = !v ? 'UNAVAILABLE' : v.available ? addLabel : 'OUT OF STOCK';
      if (idInput) { idInput.disabled = !v; if (v) idInput.value = v.id; }
      if (submit) { submit.disabled = !live; submit.style.opacity = live ? '' : '.55'; submit.textContent = label; }
      if (buybarAdd) {
        buybarAdd.disabled = !live;
        buybarAdd.style.opacity = live ? '' : '.55';
        if (v) buybarAdd.dataset.addId = v.id; else buybarAdd.removeAttribute('data-add-id');
      }
      if (buybarLabel) buybarLabel.textContent = label === addLabel ? barLabel : label;
    };

    // Variant -> gallery frame, from the map Liquid wrote above.
    const mediaMap = {};
    const mapEl = document.querySelector('[data-pdp-variant-media]');
    (mapEl ? mapEl.dataset.pdpVariantMedia : '').split(',').forEach(pair => {
      const [id, frame] = pair.split(':');
      if (id && frame !== undefined) mediaMap[id] = Number(frame);
    });

    // The same agreement on first paint as on every change: the gallery opens on the
    // frame belonging to the variant the buy box is built from, not always frame 0.
    // Matters most on a ?variant= link, where the shopper arrived asking for one.
    if (idInput && mediaMap[idInput.value] !== undefined) showImg(mediaMap[idInput.value]);

    const badge = root.querySelector('[data-pdp-badge]');
    const offer = root.querySelector('[data-pdp-offer]');
    const cmpEl = root.querySelector('[data-pdp-compare]');
    // The strikethrough, the gallery flash and the pill are three faces of one fact.
    // Only the first used to move, so the page could contradict itself.
    // Runs only on a variant change, so the deferred theme.js has defined mccSaleWas.
    const setOffer = (v) => {
      const was = window.mccSaleWas(v);
      const onSale = was > 0;
      if (cmpEl) { cmpEl.style.display = onSale ? '' : 'none'; if (onSale) cmpEl.textContent = fmt(was); }
      if (badge) badge.style.display = onSale ? '' : 'none';
      if (offer) offer.style.display = onSale ? 'inline-flex' : 'none';
    };

    sels.forEach(sel => sel.addEventListener('change', () => {
      const opts = sels.map(s => s.value);
      const v = variants.find(v => opts.every((o, i) => v.options[i] === o));
      setBuy(v);
      if (!v) return;
      const priceEl = root.querySelector('[data-pdp-price]');
      if (priceEl) priceEl.textContent = fmt(v.price);
      setOffer(v);
      const skuEl = root.querySelector('[data-pdp-sku]');
      if (skuEl && v.sku) skuEl.textContent = 'SKU ' + v.sku;
      const stockEl = root.querySelector('[data-pdp-stock]');
      if (stockEl) {
        stockEl.style.color = v.available ? 'var(--c-success)' : '#B3261E';
        stockEl.lastChild.textContent = v.available ? 'In stock — ready to ship' : 'Out of stock';
      }
      // A variant with no media of its own leaves the gallery alone rather than
      // jumping to frame 0, which would hide whatever the shopper was looking at.
      if (mediaMap[v.id] !== undefined) showImg(mediaMap[v.id]);
    }));
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product page",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "@app"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Product page"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_dynamic_checkout",
      "label": "Show accelerated checkout button (Shop Pay, Apple Pay…)",
      "info": "Lets a shopper buy this item without going through the bag.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_pharmacy_lines",
      "label": "Show the pharmacist lines on every product",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Off: the PSI-registered line, Ask a pharmacist and the PSI logo show only on products tagged with the restricted tag, or whose product type is in the Pharmacy department. On: every product. The footer's PSI logo is unaffected."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_back_in_stock",
      "label": "Show the back-in-stock request form on sold-out products",
      "default": false,
      "info": "A submission becomes one email to the store's contact address — nothing tracks inventory or emails a customer automatically. Leave off until the client confirms who owns that inbox and a live submission has been tested."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
